# AI Document Tooling Expansion — Walkthrough

## What Changed

### 5 New Document Intelligence Tools

Added to [ai_tools.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py):

| Tool | Trigger phrases | What it does |
|------|----------------|-------------|
| [summarize_document](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#679-714) | "Summarise the Week 3 slides" | Retrieves full document text (4K chars) for LLM summarisation |
| [search_across_documents](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#716-750) | "Search all modules for recursion" | Cross-course RAG query (no course filter) |
| [get_document_outline](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#752-802) | "What topics does this PDF cover?" | Extracts headings from PPTX slide titles, DOCX heading styles, PDF font-size heuristics, or text patterns |
| [extract_key_concepts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#804-840) | "Key concepts in Week 5 notes" | Returns document content (3K chars) for LLM concept extraction |
| [compare_documents](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#842-892) | "Compare Week 1 and Week 2 slides" | Fetches two files side-by-side (2K chars each) for LLM comparison |

Also added shared helper [_find_file_by_name()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/ai_tools.py#46-87) that searches across both [ModuleFile](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/module_file.py#8-25) and [CanvasFile](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/models/canvas_file.py#8-30) tables by partial filename match.

---

### RAG Improvements — [rag_service.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/rag_service.py)

- **Sentence-aware chunking**: Replaced naive 500-char slicing with [_smart_chunk()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/rag_service.py#22-61) that splits on sentence boundaries (~800 chars, 100-char overlap)
- **Section heading detection**: [_detect_section_heading()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/rag_service.py#63-79) identifies markdown headings, numbered sections, and ALL-CAPS titles
- **Enriched metadata**: Chroma now stores `chunk_index`, `total_chunks`, and [section_heading](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/rag_service.py#63-79) per chunk
- **Richer query results**: Returns [section](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/rag_service.py#63-79) and `chunk_position` fields

---

### Extraction — [extraction.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/extraction.py)

Added [extract_outline()](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/lib/extraction.py#86-191) function with native support for:
- **PPTX**: Slide title shapes
- **DOCX**: Heading paragraph styles
- **PDF**: Font-size heuristics (>13pt = heading)
- **Fallback**: Markdown `#` headings, numbered sections, ALL-CAPS lines

---

### System Prompt — [context_assembler.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/services/context_assembler.py)

Added a "Document Intelligence Tools" section to the AI's system prompt so it knows when to use each tool.

---

